"### Crypto vs TradFi in BTC regimes \u2014 beta, hedge, or divestment?\n\n**Volume-vs-BTC correlation (daily):** crypto-perp basket **-0.03**, RWA/TradFi basket **+0.00**. Crypto-perp volume only loosely tracks crypto; RWA-perp volume is far less crypto-driven.\n\n**Regime split (avg daily notional):** crypto perps do **$5.29B** in BTC-up months vs **$5.77B** in down months. RWA perps do **$1.00B** vs **$614.60M** \u2014 i.e. RWA volume still fades with crypto, but less than crypto perps do.\n\n**Fee resilience (the cash flow):** daily fees average **$2.40M** in BTC-up months vs **$2.67M** in down months \u2014 a **-11%** haircut. That is the downside the valuation carries into a bear.\n\n**Model implication:** the buyback flywheel is **crypto-beta on the way up** (more crypto volume \u2192 more fees \u2192 more burn) but partially cushioned by a **growing RWA/TradFi book that people use to rotate *out* of crypto** \u2014 so revenue is less fragile than a pure crypto-perp DEX. Weight the bear case on the fee-haircut number above, not on price beta alone.\n\n<sub>Baskets: crypto = BTC/ETH/SOL/HYPE; RWA = xyz:SP500/GOLD/SILVER/NVDA/MU/TSLA/CL + vntl:OPENAI (representative, notional = candle vol\u00d7price). RWA markets are young (from ~2026) \u2014 directional, not precise.</sub>"